<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Diamond Peak, Northside Route</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:298-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="43.604332" lon="-122.045626"><ele>1524.3</ele><name>Gold Lake Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin (OSM way 153751552 Gold Lake Sno-Park) (as in 289-2); confidence: high; pdf_page: 290; book_elev_ft: 4960; quote: ski from the far end of Gold Lake Sno-Park along a wide, uninteresting road</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.604289" lon="-122.045438"><ele>1524.9</ele><name>Road 5899 at the sno-park</name><desc>source: OSM node 2974656409 on Fores Road 5899 (Pengra Pass Road), 16 m from the pin (as in 289-2); confidence: high; pdf_page: 290</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.594370" lon="-122.059883"><ele>1511.0</ele><name>The Triangle</name><desc>source: OSM node 39789291, where roads 5899-303 and 5899-501 leave road 5899 north of Pengra Pass; 0.96 mi along 5899 (as in 289-2); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 290; quote: By continuing on the road another 0.5 mile you reach The Triangle, three short road segments forming a triangle</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.594072" lon="-122.071839"><ele>1588.6</ele><name>Midnight Lake Tie leaves road 5899</name><desc>source: OSM node 2974663920 on road 5899 near Bechtel Shelter, the north end of USFS trail 3670 Midnight Lake Tie; 1.0 mi from The Triangle (as in 289-2); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 291; quote: ski west on a road that soon becomes a trail and climbs to the Bechtel Shelter (5,120 feet)</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.586217" lon="-122.073000"><ele>1619.9</ele><name>Tie meets the PCT</name><desc>source: south end of USFS trail 3670 Midnight Lake Tie at the PCT (as in 289-2); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 291; quote: a moderate 1-mile climb through forest and meadows from the Bechtel Creek Trail</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.583182" lon="-122.075750"><ele>1648.1</ele><name>Midnight Lake</name><desc>source: OSM node 980043263 on the PCT, nearest to Midnight Lake (way 302856464) (as in 289-2); confidence: high; pdf_page: 291; book_elev_ft: 5351; quote: At 5,351 feet, Midnight Lake ... 1.7 miles from The Triangle</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.565941" lon="-122.102737"><ele>1799.6</ele><name>Blue-Haired Lady Lake (Hidden Lake)</name><desc>source: OSM node 5098992107 on the PCT, nearest to Hidden Lake (way 302856483) (as in 289-2); confidence: high; pdf_page: 291; book_elev_ft: 5840; quote: along the unmarked PCT to Blue-Haired Lady Lake (5,840 feet), called Hidden Lake on some maps</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.562782" lon="-122.109033"><ele>1837.2</ele><name>Yoran Lake Trail junction</name><desc>source: OSM node 980043097, Yoran Lake Trail meets the PCT (as in 289-2); confidence: high; pdf_page: 291</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.557366" lon="-122.106455"><ele>1823.6</ele><name>Yoran Lake (north end)</name><desc>source: OSM node 6785194442 on Yoran Lake Trail at the lake's north end; lake unnamed in OSM, found as the flat 5,947 ft DEM surface at 43.555, -122.106 (as in 289-2); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 291; book_elev_ft: 6000; quote: Ski another 0.7 mile to Yoran Lake south of the PCT at 6,000 feet</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.558500" lon="-122.110000"><ele>1828.4</ele><name>North-west shore of Yoran Lake</name><desc>source: DEM 5,999 ft, above the 5,947 ft lake surface, so the leg to the saddle does not cross the lake; confidence: low; pdf_page: 300; quote: map 71: dotted line from Yoran Lk to the saddle by Mt Yoran</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.548407" lon="-122.133449"><ele>2073.3</ele><name>Leave the PCT at the saddle (6,800 ft)</name><desc>source: OSM node 980042985 on the PCT, DEM 6,802 ft, between Mt Yoran and Diamond Peak; 1.6 mi from Yoran Lake (map 71: 1.5); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 300; book_elev_ft: 6800; quote: map 71: SADDLE 6800'</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.547000" lon="-122.147500"><ele>2145.8</ele><name>Foot of the northwest ridge</name><desc>source: DEM: lowest end of the ridge crest that runs south to the north summit; confidence: low; pdf_page: 300; quote: Ski to the northwest ridge of Diamond Peak and ascend this</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.542000" lon="-122.145000"><ele>2285.1</ele><name>Ridge 7,500 ft</name><desc>source: DEM ridge crest; confidence: low; pdf_page: 300</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.536000" lon="-122.143000"><ele>2392.1</ele><name>Ridge 7,850 ft</name><desc>source: DEM ridge crest; confidence: low; pdf_page: 300</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.533000" lon="-122.141000"><ele>2479.0</ele><name>Ridge 8,130 ft</name><desc>source: DEM ridge crest; confidence: low; pdf_page: 300</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.528500" lon="-122.146000"><ele>2622.7</ele><name>North end of the summit ridge</name><desc>source: DEM 8,600 ft knob; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 300; quote: ascend this to the long summit ridge, which narrows as you ski</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.524000" lon="-122.147000"><ele>2574.9</ele><name>Summit ridge</name><desc>source: DEM crest; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 300; quote: climb southward to the highest point</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.520703" lon="-122.149610"><ele>2666.0</ele><name>Diamond Peak summit</name><desc>source: OSM node 1691537555 Diamond Peak; confidence: high; pdf_page: 300; book_elev_ft: 8744; quote: map 71: DIAMOND PK 8744'</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Diamond Peak, Northside Route</name><desc>1. Gold Lake Sno-Park -&gt; Road 5899 at the sno-park: straight (high), 0.01 mi | 2. Road 5899 at the sno-park -&gt; The Triangle: osm (high), 1.05 mi | 3. The Triangle -&gt; Midnight Lake Tie leaves road 5899: osm (medium), 0.99 mi | 4. Midnight Lake Tie leaves road 5899 -&gt; Tie meets the PCT: usfs-trail (medium), 0.64 mi | 5. Tie meets the PCT -&gt; Midnight Lake: osm (high), 0.27 mi | 6. Midnight Lake -&gt; Blue-Haired Lady Lake (Hidden Lake): osm (medium), 2.48 mi | 7. Blue-Haired Lady Lake (Hidden Lake) -&gt; Yoran Lake Trail junction: osm (high), 0.43 mi | 8. Yoran Lake Trail junction -&gt; Yoran Lake (north end): osm (medium), 0.45 mi | 9. Yoran Lake (north end) -&gt; North-west shore of Yoran Lake: straight (low), 0.19 mi | 10. North-west shore of Yoran Lake -&gt; Leave the PCT at the saddle (6,800 ft): straight (low), 1.37 mi | 11. Leave the PCT at the saddle (6,800 ft) -&gt; Foot of the northwest ridge: straight (low), 0.71 mi | 12. Foot of the northwest ridge -&gt; Ridge 7,500 ft: straight (low), 0.37 mi | 13. Ridge 7,500 ft -&gt; Ridge 7,850 ft: straight (low), 0.43 mi | 14. Ridge 7,850 ft -&gt; Ridge 8,130 ft: straight (low), 0.23 mi | 15. Ridge 8,130 ft -&gt; North end of the summit ridge: straight (medium), 0.40 mi | 16. North end of the summit ridge -&gt; Summit ridge: straight (medium), 0.31 mi | 17. Summit ridge -&gt; Diamond Peak summit: straight (medium), 0.26 mi</desc>
